Bugfix: accept rustic-style TOML profile aliases

Vaultic TOML profiles now accept the rustic deployment spelling used by common
repository configurations: `[repository].repository`, `set-compression`,
`packsize-default`, and `packsize-tree`; `[global].group-by`; and backup/job
`globs` with `!` exclusion entries. TOML arrays are applied as repeated flags,
so `exclude-if-present` and glob exclusions work as expected for named backup
jobs. Named jobs also correctly preserve the documented precedence of explicit
CLI scalar flags over per-job and shared backup profile values.

